==Strategy==
The main difficulty of this stage comes from its restriction. Due to Wahwah's 1000 range Omni Strikes, 100% knockback chance and fast attack cycle consisting of three closely-spaced multi-hits, [[:Category:Normal Cats|Normal]] units have no hope of ever defeating Wahwah nor the peons unless they are highly leveled and supported by Defense Up [[Cat Combo]]s. [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber]] and [[:Category:Legend Rare Cats|Legend Rare]]s, the only other units allowed, stand a better chance, although the most useful ones for the stage are tankers and rushers, preferably with low cooldown timers, and will be key to even the Abyssal version, where players cannot reuse the same unit in their formation. Fortunately, only the "weak" peons respawn, and most strategies focus on outlasting the stronger ones, eventually leaving Wahwah with little to no support.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
Your Normal Cats should at least be +40 or higher on average depending on your Uber Super Rares, barring Mohawk Cat.
*[[Cat (Normal Cat)|Mohawk]]/[[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Eraser]] - Basic meatshields to provide support by stalling the peons while other units catch up.
*[[Titan Cat (Normal Cat)|Jamiera Cat]] and [[Fish Cat (Normal Cat)|Island Cat]] - Can survive Wahwah's attacks and deal damage in between peon waves. Bring them if you lack good Tanker-Class Ubers.
*[[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|King Dragon Cat]] - A good midranger dealing decent damage from a high range, though only bring him if you don't own good midrangers.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
For general attackers:
*[[Kasa Jizo (Uber Rare Cat)|Kasa Jizo]]: In his normal and ultra form, Jizo is a fast, cheap and disposable midranger with Massive Damage to Darks, which destroys Shadow Boxer K and Doge Dark. Packing decent stats as well, Jizo has many opportunities to hit Wahwah once the peons are clear. In ultra form, he can even solo the stage for abyssal clears.
*[[Baby Gao (Uber Rare Cat)|Baby Gao]], [[D'artanyan (Uber Rare Cat)|D'artanyan]], [[Child of Destiny Phono (Uber Rare Cat)|Child of Destiny Phono]]: Much more preferable in their first forms, they provide good damage to the Kang Roos at a spammable cooldown and decent cost, similar to Jizo.
*[[Lesser Demon Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Greater Balrog Cat]]: With a very fast cooldown and somewhat low cost for a uber, Greater Balrog's melee range and single target attacks are generally not problematic, given the overall lack of peons, and more can be fielded if one is lost. Greater Balrog's strengthen talents aren't necessary, but can give some extra punch on his final knockback to hopefully kill the strong peons.
*[[Sanada Yukimura (Uber Rare Cat)|Immortal Yukimura]]: Yukimura's very high speed makes timing easy and he has enough base damage to knockback Wahwah in one hit. His Massive Damage to Dark can nuke Shadow Boxer K.
*[[Momotaro (Uber Rare Cat)|The Peach Devils]]: Can rush up to King Wahwah and deal decent chip damage while lasting somewhat long thanks to their decent health.
*[[Iz the Dancer of Grief (Uber Rare Cat)|Iz The Dancer Of Grief]]: A very helpful unit to own for this stage as her powerful anti-Traitless attacks can knockback Wahwah with every hit. She also has Zombie Killer and Knockback Immunity. If she dies she can easily be replaced because of her short cooldown.
*[[Thunder Jack (Uber Rare Cat)|Bloody Jack]]: Jack is a fast rusher with only one knockback, rapid Single Attack Multi-Hits and a 50% chance to knockback Aliens/Zombies in his evolved form. Considering the sporadic peon spawns and his relatively low cooldown, Jack can not only wipe them out quickly but also yield significant damage on Wahwah.
*[[Baby Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Cats in the Cradle]]: A melee unit with very high damage, great disposability and level 2 wave attacks, Cradle can easily cripple peons and knock Wahwah away on hit. Despite being vulnerable to knockback, Cradle's health allows it to last several cycles and potentially reach the boss.
*[[Mighty Sphinx Korps (Uber Rare Cat)|Hyper Battalion Convoys]]: The unit tanks and rebounds off hits, unleashing wave attacks with each rebound, all of which tend to hit Wahwah doing a lot of damage and reclaiming ground.
*[[Trixi the Merc (Uber Rare Cat)|Trixi the Merc]]: With her Strong against Traitless and Aliens and chance to Freeze them briefly, she performs excellently here. Her rapid attacks will juggle the peons, allowing her to walk up to Wahwah and knock him back all the way to the base. Getting her to Lv.32 is recommended, since it allows her to knockback a Doge Dark in only 1 attack cycle, which greatly improves her survivability.

For specialist attackers:
*[[Issun Boshi (Uber Rare Cat)|Issun Boshi]]: With high speed, massive damage against Traitless, and a low cost of 675c, Boshi can be used as a source of chip damage between peon waves to gradually kill King Wahwah. Do note that its range is pitiful, so do not send it out when peons are in front of Wahwah.
*[[Izanami of Dusk (Legend Rare Cat)|Izanami of Dusk]]: If you are lucky enough to have her, Izanami's extreme damage against Traitless enemies can wipe out Wahwah in a matter of hits.
*[[Bora (Uber Rare Cat)|Bazibastra]]: Destroys Scissoroo, and can still provide some contribution to the other Kang Roos, though with less effectiveness. His cooldown and price are rather low for an Uber, too, and his bulk allows him to survive Wahwah for a decent amount of time.
*[[Mighty Aethur Ltd. (Uber Rare Cat)|Ultra Atlantis Logistix]]: Absolutely obliterates Zang Roo, who is arguably the most problematic Roo in the stage. Can also be used alongside [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]] if you need the combo, otherwise use a Rich Cat. Do note that it is terrible against anything else, so only use Logistix for Zang Roo.
*[[Bliza (Uber Rare Cat)|Blizarena]]: Great for Scissoroo and Zang Roo, though she trades damage for higher health and crowd-control capabilities compared to Bazibastra and Logistix.
*[[D'arktanyan (Uber Rare Cat)|Valiant D'arktanyan]]: At level 32, he can just barely survive 4 attack cycles from King Wahwah, and will strengthen after 2 or 3 cycles. His absurd amounts of damage and DPS against Traitless allows him to rush down and nuke Wahwah fairly easily. However, timing D'arktanyan is necessary due to his lack of Knockback Immunity.
*[[Shadow Gao (Uber Rare Cat)|Diabolic Gao]]: Thanks to his Immunity to Knockback and Massive Damage against Traitless, he will easily shred a large chunk of health off of King Wahwah if he is given the chance. Getting even a few hits on him can completely change the flow of battle, so do your best to protect him from the peons.

For tankers:
*[[Gravi (Uber Rare Cat)|Gravolodon]]: Anti-Alien tank with a somewhat fast cooldown and powerful [[Wave Attack]]s that can reach Wahwah by hitting the peons. If boosted by [[Catseye]]s and "Unit Attack UP" Combos, it could knock Wahwah back in just one or two hits and regain ground. A level 40 Gravolodon deals just shy of that amount (39820<40000), so only one damage-up combo is needed for it to bully Wahwah. Furthermore, with talents, it gains Knockback Immunity, preventing it from being pushed back.
*[[Kai (Uber Rare Cat)|Divine Kai μ]]: Divine Kai μ's disposability, knockback immunity, massive base HP and high burst damage at point-blank range allow her to nearly carry the stage, being able to solo Wahwah without his support. Since the Kang Roo variants don't come often and also have short range, she can also be used to pick them off.
*[[Cat Machine (Uber Rare Cat)|Cat Machine Mk 3]]: With the knockback immunity [[Talents|Talent]], Cat Machine Mk 3 can absorb many hits and stall Wahwah, while dealing great damage. Its recharge time is also relatively short for a tank, allowing more to be sent over the same timeframe and reducing the chances of Wahwah overwhelming you.
*[[Urashima Taro (Uber Rare Cat)|King Gamereon]]: His low speed and naturally high HP allows him to stay in the backline after getting knocked back by Wahwah, ensuring a good defense against the peons, even outside of his targeted traits.
*[[Lumina (Legend Rare Cat)|Luminalia]]: Luminalia is a fast anti-Alien tank that has decent damage, high health and a mildly fast cooldown. When boosted with Catseyes, Luminalia is a powerful unit on this stage; at level 40, she has over 170,000 health and has enough damage to knockback Wahwah with a single hit. She can obliterate the Scissoroo with ease and also handle the other peons thanks to her solid stats and relatively fast cooldown. Unfortunately, Luminalia is a Legend Rare, so obtaining her or the Legend Catseyes needed to upgrade her to level 40 are far more difficult than the other units listed above.
*[[Hades the Punisher (Uber Rare Cat)|Almighty Hades]]: A good generalist tanker with [[Immune to Knockback|Knockback Immunity]]. Due to the mixed nature of this stage, he will outperform specialist tankers. His high attack rate and respectable DPS also help with clearing the peons. While generally unusable outside of his True Form, which requires an [[Epic Catfruit Seed]], he will prove to be invaluable on your [[Abyssal Stage]] attempts, where options are incredibly limited.
For general support:
*[[Asiluga (Uber Rare Cat)|Assassinlan Pasalan]] - With a 100% chance to slow all enemies for 3 seconds over a whopping 1250 standing range, a well-positioned Assassinlan Pasalan can evade all of Wahwah's attacks and provide occasional support, though it shouldn't be the only source of damage.

